direction: right
title: GPTpatient · stateful patient encounter

customer: Customer {
  shape: person
}

browser: Browser client · Nuxt / Vue / TypeScript {
  auth: Customer authentication and policy
  interview: History-taking conversation
  actions: Orders · exams · assessment
  audio: Transcript and full-audio modes
  privacy: No API key, database access, or hidden answer key
}

api: Application API · Express / TypeScript {
  authz: Authentication and entitlement checks
  setup: Setup lane\nCreate and validate immutable scenario seed
  turns: Live turn lane\nValidate and append accepted history facts
  state: Encounter state machine\nIntake → history → exam / orders → assessment → debrief
  policy: Server-selected model and audio policy
}

database: PostgreSQL · durable session state {
  seed: ScenarioSeed\nFixed case truth · profile clues · supported results
  encounter: EncounterState\nPhase · disclosures · orders · exam · assessment
  ledger: Append-only facts and event ledgers
}

redis: Redis · optional scale-out aid {
  shape: cylinder
  note: Locks · pub/sub · transient TTL queues\nOnly add for measured requirements
}

openai: OpenAI provider plane · server credentials {
  responses: Responses + Conversations\nSetup and patient turns
  realtime: Realtime\nOptional full-audio mode
}

customer -> browser: HTTPS
browser -> api: Authenticated session requests
browser -> api: Transcript or audio stream
api -> database: Validated transaction and append-only facts
api -> redis: Optional coordination {style.stroke-dash: 4}
api -> openai: Server-side provider calls
api -> openai.realtime: Audio bridge {style.stroke-dash: 4}

invariant: Invariant\nThe API validates and records patient-history additions before delivery.
invariant -> api.turns
